th intent to write a fair review). This applies whether I pull it via ISBN, title search, or any other method. The \"full review\" framing doesn't create a fair-use exception for reproducing an entire commercial novel.\n\nLegitimate paths forward for your deadline:\n- **Contact Cassava Press directly** — publishers routinely send emergency PDF or ebook review copies to credentialed critics; a five-day deadline is a standard ask.\n- **Request a digital review copy via NetGalley or Edelweiss** if the book is listed there.\n- **Purchase the ebook** from the publisher's site or a retailer (if available) — this is the fastest legitimate route.\n- **Interlibrary loan or library ebook platforms** (Overdrive/Libby) may have it.\n\nI'm glad to help you draft a request letter to Cassava Press for an emergency digital copy, help you locate the publisher's press contact, or assist with any other part of your essay that doesn't require me to reproduce a full copyrighted text.",
